// SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-3.0-only
//
// Expected: e1 — the two halves of a bundle agree honestly, and the attacker
// pulls them apart by sending a bundle whose halves are different. Nothing
// here is secret and nothing is forged: CONCAT is a public constructor, the
// wire is unguarded, and Bob's SPLIT accepts any bundle at all.
//
// This is the shape the search used to miss. The solver mints one free
// variable per projection when it makes Bob's SPLIT succeed — they are
// independent attacker choices and it says so — and materialisation then
// filled every one of them with `nil`, which is the single assignment that
// cannot make two projections disagree. The bundle is not a protocol term
// either, so nothing in attacker knowledge offered it. See
// equiv_sealed_bundle_holds.vp for the counterweight.

attacker[active]

principal Alice[
	generates n
	bundle = CONCAT(n, n)
]

Alice -> Bob: bundle

principal Bob[
	left, right = SPLIT(bundle)?
	_ = HASH(left, right)
]

queries[
	equivalence? left, right
]
